<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali-Qoli Khan Bakhtiari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1858">1858</a>–<a href="/years/1917">1917</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sardar As'ad II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali-Qoli Khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhtiari">Bakhtiari</a>, known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardar">Sardar</a> As'ad II, was a chief of the Bakhtiari tribes of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and a supporter of the Constitutional Revolution. In 1909 he and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najaf-qoli-khan-bakhtiari">Samsam al-Saltaneh</a> led Bakhtiari forces to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a>, deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammad-ali-shah-qajar">Mohammad Ali Shah</a> and restored the constitution. He then served as minister of the interior, and the Bakhtiari khans shared in oil revenues from their lands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ali-qoli-khan-bakhtiari.jpg" alt="Ali-Qoli Khan Bakhtiari" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alasvand.saam · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sardar.asad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
